
Sourcetrail
===========

Usage
-----

Run the Sourcetrail.sh script to start Sourcetrail.

Command line: bin/st indexes a project (st index [--full]) and answers code navigation queries over its index
(callers, implementations, paths, impact; see "st: code navigation for agents" in the project README). It starts
bin/sourcetrail to index, so keep them in the same directory.

TypeScript (an Angular + Spring app in one folder, or a TypeScript-only project) needs Node.js 22.13 or newer on PATH
and the project's node_modules (run npm install in the project first). Without them the Java still indexes and the
TypeScript step reports why it was skipped.


Install
-------

Run install.sh to install Sourcetrail to /opt/sourcetrail
It also creates a symlink named 'sourcetrail' in /usr/bin to launch Sourcetrail from the console.
Root permission is required to run this script.

Run uninstall.sh to uninstall Sourcetrail.


User Data Files
---------------

Sourcetrail places user data files at ~/.config/sourcetrail
Run resetPreferences.sh to delete them and reset Sourcetrail to the initial configuration.


